Eludite @VERSION@ for @OS@ (@ARCH@)
====================================

Run it from this folder:

    eludite@EXE@ --folder path/to/my-project        (or --solution path/to/App.slnx)

Nothing here needs installing, and Eludite needs no environment variables: the shell finds the programs it runs beside
itself (Companions, below). Eludite makes no network call at startup.

This archive has no embedded browser engine, which runs on Linux only so far (the Linux tarball carries it): the Web
Browser window says so when opened. The eludite.browser.* commands still drive a Chrome found on the machine or named
by ELUDITE_CHROME.

Files
-----

    eludite@EXE@               the IDE
    eludite-host/              the .NET host
    eludite-dbg-mono/          the .NET Framework debugger for Mono
    eludite-claude-acp@EXE@    the Claude Code adapter
    LICENSE                    GNU General Public License, version 3 (Eludite is GPL-3.0-or-later)
    THIRD-PARTY-CRATES.txt     the Rust crates linked into eludite, with their licenses
    licenses/                  the companions' licenses
